cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Plugin Value Lab, cite this software and identify the exact release
  or commit used. For an unreleased checkout, include the commit and local
  modifications. A software citation does not establish scientific validation.
type: software
title: Plugin Value Lab
authors:
  - name: Plugin Value Lab contributors
repository-code: https://github.com/HERRY423/Plugin-Value-Lab
url: https://github.com/HERRY423/Plugin-Value-Lab
version: 0.9.0
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Determine whether a plugin improves a specific task through paired comparisons,
  frozen plans, and recomputable results. Compare original with-plugin and
  no-plugin records under matched conditions; retain failures, uncertainty and
  missing evidence. Conclusions remain scoped to the tested task and conditions.
keywords:
  - research software
  - plugin evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - evidence governance
